{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And He gave, etc., when He finished.</b> One needs to know why the verse interrupted between the mention of the giving and the mention of the thing given by the statement of the time — for it should have said, ״וַיִּתֵּן אֶל מֹשֶׁה שְׁנֵי לוּחוֹת כְּכַלּוֹתוֹ״, or it should have placed ״כְּכַלּוֹתוֹ״ before the mention of the giving. Further, one must note why HaShem delayed the giving of the tablets until this time, since they contained nothing but the Ten Commandments — on the day of the giving of the Torah or on the morrow He should have given the tablets?" "Now the matter will be clarified according to the words of our Sages of blessed memory (Zohar 2:93a) who said that all the commandments are surely contained within the Ten Commandments. And this is what the verse says: <b>And He gave to Moses, when He finished speaking with him on Mount Sinai</b>, and what did He speak with him? <b>Two tablets of the testimony</b> — meaning that the matters inscribed in the tablets, the supreme El set for him, and it was not fitting to give him the tablets until He completed what is inscribed in them. Therefore He completed the matters alluded to in the tablets of the testimony and then gave them to him, and not before. With this, both fine points are resolved at once correctly. And according to this, the phrase ״two tablets״ continues both from ״when He finished speaking with him״ etc., and continues from ״and He gave״ stated at the beginning of the verse." "<b>Written with the finger of Elohim.</b> The intention here, according to the words of our Sages of blessed memory (Tanhuma, Eikev), is that the tablets were hewn from beneath the Throne of His Glory, may He be blessed. Or perhaps this is what is alluded to in the verse saying ״מַעֲשֵׂה אֱלֹהִים״ — meaning, the work of [Elohim] is the Throne; and understand. And it has already been explained that there are many levels of the lights of holiness in the sod of (Ecclesiastes 5:7) ״כִּי גָבוֹהַּ מֵעַל גָבוֹהַּ וְגוֹ׳ וּגְבוֹהִים״, and go forth and learn from the wondrous matter brought in the holy Zohar (Zohar 2:52a): when Moses ascended on high and encountered the angel Sandalfon etc., and afterward the angel Metatron, and he was afraid of the angel because of the fire of that which was above him, lest it consume him, and so forth. And behold, the verse says (Deuteronomy 4:24) ״כִּי ה׳ אֱלֹהֶיךָ אֵשׁ אוֹכְלָה הוּא״ — for His holy fire consumes every fire other than it." "And the verse informed us of the manner of the writing of the tablets, in what they were written, and it says <b>written with the finger of Elohim</b> — meaning that HaShem would trace the form of the letter with His finger, as it were, meaning one aspect of light from His light, may He be blessed, in the likeness of a finger opposite the tablet, according to the measure of the surface area of the limbs of the letters, so that there would be engraving only of that which He traced opposite it. And given the overwhelming intensity of His light, may He be blessed, the light of the tablets could not endure in every place toward which the finger of Elohim was directed, but would be consumed or else contract to the sides, and whatever was traced opposite it remained hollowed out. Therefore they were inscribed from both their sides, and this is what the verse says (Exodus 32:16) ״חָרוּת עַל הַלֻּחֹת״ — and it does not say חָרוּת בַּלּוּחוֹת, which would convey that He made the engraving in the tablets, but rather עַל — meaning that the Holy One, blessed be He, would place His finger upon the tablets in the likeness of the form of the letter, and in this manner the letters of the Ten Commandments were engraved."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {3 "ה׳ in comment [0] resolved as HaShem based on context (divine act of giving the tablets); in [3] likewise. In [1] and [3], אל עליון and the Blessed One rendered with standard reverent forms."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:35:29.265467429Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}